    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34315": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business Administration",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Professor of Business Administration Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Professor of Business Administration Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a letter of application addressing your qualifications for this position, a statement of teaching philosophy, a statement of research interests and experience, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin October 27, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34300 . Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Professor of Business Administration Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Kokomo School of Business Location Kokomo Position Summary The School of Business at Indiana University Kokomo invites applications for a full-time, 10-month, Assistant Professor of Business Administration beginning Spring/Fall 2027. Information about the program can be found at https://kokomo.iu.edu/business/index.html . Responsibilities include teaching three courses per semester; establishing and maintaining an active, productive research program; and being active in service to the program, the campus, and the university. One of eight campuses of Indiana University, Indiana University Kokomo is a comprehensive non-residential campus located 50 miles north of Indianapolis in Kokomo, Indiana, a city with a population of about 57,000. Committed to student success, the campus serves approximately 3,230 students from a 14-county area in north-central Indiana. lU Kokomo has around 260 full-time faculty and staff. Associate, baccalaureate, and master’s degrees are offered. Additional information about Indiana University Kokomo can be accessed at http://Kokomo.iu.edu/ . Accommodations are available in the hiring process for individuals with disabilities. Those needing accommodation should contact the Office of Civil Rights Compliance at 765-455-9316. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer, and a provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Basic Qualifications Requirements include a doctoral degree in Management or a closely related field, teaching experience at the undergraduate college level, and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in student-centered learning and collaboration. ABD will be considered. We seek candidates with a strong commitment to teaching, research, and service. A focus in one of the following areas is preferred – MIS , Accounting, Business Analytics, or Finance. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to tbutler@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applicants should submit a letter of application addressing your qualifications for this position, a statement of teaching philosophy, a statement of research interests and experience, curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin October 27, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34300 . For Best Consideration Date 10/26/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101674-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
