    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34170": {
      "title": "Associate Dean and Professor of Education",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Associate Dean and Professor of Education Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Associate Dean and Professor of Education Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a letter of application addressing your qualifications for this position, a curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34168 . Posting Details Position Details Title Associate Dean and Professor of Education Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Kokomo Division of Education Location Kokomo Position Summary The Division of Education at Indiana University Kokomo invites applications for a full time, 10-month, Associate Dean position beginning January 1, 2027. The Associate Dean reports to the Dean of the School of Humanities and Social Sciences, and the position includes a faculty rank of associate or full professor, depending on qualifications. Information about the program can be found at https://www.iuk.edu/humanities-and-social-sciences/education/index.html . One of eight campuses of Indiana University, Indiana University Kokomo is a comprehensive non-residential campus located 50 miles north of Indianapolis in Kokomo, Indiana, a city with a population of about 57,000. Committed to student success, the campus serves approximately 3,230 students from a 14-county area in north-central Indiana. IU Kokomo has around 260 full-time faculty and staff. Associate, baccalaureate, and master’s degrees are offered. Additional information about Indiana University Kokomo can be accessed at http://www.iuk.edu . Accommodations are available in the hiring process for individuals with disabilities. Those needing accommodations should contact the Office of Civil Rights Compliance at 765-455-9316. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer, and a provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Basic Qualifications Requirements include a doctoral degree in Education or related field, teaching experience at the undergraduate college level, a successful research program, a demonstrated commitment to collaboration, and administrative experience. The candidate’s teaching, research, and service record will be appropriate for the rank of associate or full professor at Indiana University Kokomo. Teaching and/or research experience in literacy is preferred, but not required. Administrative duties The associate dean will primarily serve an administrative role and will also have faculty status within the Division of Education. Administrative duties include: Operational oversight, e.g. working closely with placement coordinator, program coordinator, and assessment coordinator. Represent IUK DOE on multiple committees, such as the MSEd in Science of Reading and Registered Apprenticeship program. Oversee curriculum, enrollment, recruitment, retention, advising, and student progression across undergraduate, graduate, licensure, residency, and apprenticeship programs. Lead accreditation, assessment, and regulatory compliance, including CAEP accreditation, Teacher Preparation Inspection, state policies, licensure requirements, and key program assessments. Develop, launch, and revise academic programs in response to workforce needs, state mandates, enrollment trends, and student outcomes. Hire, onboard, train, mentor, and evaluate adjunct instructors, including syllabus review, teaching observations, feedback meetings, and ongoing instructional support. Build and maintain partnerships with P–12 districts, superintendents, state agencies, IU Online, other IU campuses, and external organizations. Represent the Division of Education on campus, university, state, and cross-campus committees and serve as a primary point of contact for external partners. Lead recruitment, outreach, and program promotion through district visits, information sessions, campus events, website updates, and marketing materials. Teaching and service Teach one course per semester. Summer teaching is optional and for additional pay. Perform various service duties for the Division. Research Tenured and tenure-track faculty have research expectations governed by Division, campus, and university policies. Normally this is 20% of their workload, but administrative positions waive this requirement. Should the associate dean leave the administrative position and return to faculty, they will be expected to pursue a research agenda in accordance with these policies. Workload The associate dean’s workload will follow Indiana University’s standard formula as follows: 60% admin 20% teaching 20% service Compensation includes faculty salary (dependent on rank) and an administrative stipend throughout the 10-month academic year as well as during summer sessions. Summer teaching is optional and for additional pay. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to Sharon Johnson, Division of Education, Indiana University Kokomo, shrjohn@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applicants should submit a letter of application addressing your qualifications for this position, a curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/34168 . For Best Consideration Date 10/01/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101650-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you previously been employed with IU? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33820": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructors in the Bachelor of Science and Masters of Science in Nursing Program",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Adjunct Instructors in the Bachelor of Science and Masters of Science in Nursing Program Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Adjunct Instructors in the Bachelor of Science and Masters of Science in Nursing Program Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please provide: A cover letter describing teaching philosophy, instructional methods, and technologies relevant to your teaching experience. Include any qualifications not evident in your resume or curriculum vitae. A resume/CV summarizing your educational background and industry and teaching experience. Transcripts. Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness – Teaching Evaluations/Teaching Awards. The names and contact information of three references. Posting Details Position Details Title Adjunct Instructors in the Bachelor of Science and Masters of Science in Nursing Program Appointment Status Non-Tenure Track Department IU Kokomo School of Nursing and Allied Health Professions Location Kokomo Position Summary The Bachelor of Science and the Masters of Science in Nursing Programs in the School of Nursing and Allied Health Professions are seeking applications to build a pool of adjunct instructors for possible future part-time course assignments.  The ideal candidate will have experience teaching lecture and laboratory courses, as well as experience in utilizing the virtual environment, such as Canvas LMS , to augment classroom instruction. Preference will be given to candidates who have relevant teaching and practice experience. Application review will begin immediately and continue until all available vacancies have been filled. One of eight campuses of Indiana University, Indiana University Kokomo, is a comprehensive non-residential campus located 50 miles north of Indianapolis in Kokomo, Indiana, a city with a population of about 57,000. Committed to student success, the campus serves approximately 3,230 students from a 14-county area in north-central Indiana. IU Kokomo has around 260 full-time faculty and staff. Associate, baccalaureate, and master’s degrees are offered. Additional information about Indiana University Kokomo can be accessed at http://www.iuk.edu. Accommodations are available in the hiring process for individuals with disabilities. Those needing accommodations should contact the Office of Civil Rights Compliance at 765-455-9316. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer, and a provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Basic Qualifications Applicants must be a licensed registered nurse in the State of Indiana, hold an MSN degree awarded by an institution that is accredited by the CNEA , CCNE , or ACEN , and have at least 3 years of practice experience. Possible courses could include but are not limited to: Administrative Management in Nursing Advanced Health Assessment Advanced Pathophysiology Advanced Pharmacology Advanced Role/Concepts Clinical courses/Practicums/Labs Evaluation in Nursing Financial Management Healthcare Quality and Safety/Performance Improvement Informatics Legal Environment of Care Nursing Leadership Nursing Research Nursing Theory Population Health Primary Care Courses Primary Office Procedures Teaching in Nursing Required Documents: 1. Curriculum Vitae 2. Letter of Application 3. Evidence of Teaching Ability 4. Transcript 5. List Of References Department Contact for Questions If you have any questions, please contact Candace Kirk, Executive Assistant to the Dean, School of Nursing and Allied Health Professions, Indiana University Kokomo, 2300 S. Washington St., Kokomo, IN 46902. Email: kirkcand@iu.edu , Phone: 765-455-9288. Please apply at link: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/31695 . Additional Qualifications Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in nursing. Salary and Rank Special Instructions Please provide: A cover letter describing teaching philosophy, instructional methods, and technologies relevant to your teaching experience. Include any qualifications not evident in your resume or curriculum vitae. A resume/CV summarizing your educational background and industry and teaching experience. Transcripts. Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness – Teaching Evaluations/Teaching Awards. The names and contact information of three references. For Best Consideration Date 07/20/2026 Expected Start Date 08/01/2026 Posting Number IU-101445-2025 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability List Of References Transcript Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33799": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Indiana University Academic Positions | Assistant Professor of Accounting Skip to Main Content Academic Careers at IU Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus IU Bloomington>> IU Indianapolis>> IU East>> IU Kokomo>> IU Northwest>> IU South Bend>> IU Southeast>> IU Columbus>> IU Fort Wayne>> IU School of Medicine>> Assistant Professor of Accounting Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer and provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report, containing policy statements, crime and fire statistics for all Indiana University campuses, is available online . You may also request a physical copy by emailing IU Public Safety at iups@iu.edu Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a letter of application addressing your qualifications for this position given the requirements and preferences above. The letter should include a short summary of teaching experience and philosophy, a statement of research interests and publications (if any), and professional experience (if any). In addition to the letter, include evidence of teaching effectiveness (original course evaluations), curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33795 . Posting Details Position Details Title Assistant Professor of Accounting Appointment Status Tenure Track Department IU Kokomo School of Business Location Kokomo Position Summary The School of Business at Indiana University Kokomo invites applications for a full-time, 10-month, Assistant Professor of Accounting position beginning Spring/Fall 2027. Information about the program can be found at https://kokomo.iu.edu/business/index.html . The Assistant Professor of Accounting is responsible for teaching undergraduate and graduate accounting courses (in-person, hybrid, and online), maintaining an active research agenda, and contributing to service activities at the department, school, university, and professional levels. The position supports the academic mission of the institution, including maintaining high standards aligned with AACSB accreditation expectations. One of eight campuses of Indiana University, Indiana University Kokomo is a comprehensive non-residential campus located 50 miles north of Indianapolis in Kokomo, Indiana, a city with a population of about 57,000. Committed to student success, the campus serves approximately 3,230 students from a 14-county area in north-central Indiana. lU Kokomo has around 260 full-time faculty and staff. Associate, baccalaureate, and master’s degrees are offered. Additional information about Indiana University Kokomo can be accessed at http://Kokomo.iu.edu/ . Accommodations are available in the hiring process for individuals with disabilities. Those needing accommodation should contact the Office of Civil Rights Compliance at 765-455-9316. Indiana University is an equal opportunity employer, and a provider of ADA services and prohibits discrimination in hiring. See Indiana University Notice of Non-Discrimination here which includes contact information. Basic Qualifications Minimum Qualifications A doctoral degree in accounting or a closely related field (if the applicant holds CPA certification), teaching experience at the college level with evidence of a commitment to student-focused approach, and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in student-centered teaching. ABD will be considered. We seek candidates with a strong commitment to teaching, research, and service. Department Contact for Questions Questions regarding the position or application process can be directed to tbutler@iu.edu . Additional Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Beyond the minimum qualifications identified above, preference will be given to applicants with a doctoral degree from an AACSB accredited university, teaching awards or other evidence of excellence in teaching, professional accounting or finance work experience, CPA , CMA , or other professional accounting certifications, and/or a record of scholarly publications. Salary and Rank Special Instructions Applicants should submit a letter of application addressing your qualifications for this position given the requirements and preferences above. The letter should include a short summary of teaching experience and philosophy, a statement of research interests and publications (if any), and professional experience (if any). In addition to the letter, include evidence of teaching effectiveness (original course evaluations), curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should review the application requirements and submit their application at: https://indiana.peopleadmin.com/postings/33795 . For Best Consideration Date 09/01/2026 Expected Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Number IU-101608-2026 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Evidence of Teaching Ability Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research and Teaching List Of References Optional Documents Copyright © 2026 The Trustees of Indiana University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
